# Flight modes for a THREE-position switch (FS-i6 SwC on channel 5), for an
# aircraft whose COMPASS AND GPS ARE NOT YET PROVEN.
#
# A 3-position switch cannot reach six slots. At the usual 1000/1500/2000 us
# it lands in slots 1, 4 and 6, so those are the only three that matter and
# the rest repeat their neighbour -- PWM drift across a boundary then changes
# nothing. CONFIRM with ./mode_monitor.py: endpoint and subtrim settings move
# the actual PWM, and if your switch lands in different slots this mapping is
# wrong for your radio.
#
#   slot 1  STABILIZE  manual, always available
#   slot 4  ALT_HOLD   holds height, still manual horizontally
#   slot 6  LAND       descend here, now
#
# LAND rather than RTL deliberately. RTL flies a compass bearing home at
# altitude: with an uncalibrated compass it does that confidently in the
# wrong direction. LAND needs neither heading nor position. Switch to
# 51-fltmodes-3pos-rtl.params once the compass is calibrated and the GPS has
# been seen to hold a 3D fix outdoors.
FLTMODE1,0
FLTMODE2,0
FLTMODE3,2
FLTMODE4,2
FLTMODE5,9
FLTMODE6,9
FLTMODE_CH,5
